# Supabase & Next.js Pre-Launch Security Guardrails

Apply this checklist before deploying AI-assisted Next.js, React, Vite, or Supabase applications to production. Keep checks read-only unless explicitly asked to apply a migration or config change.

## 1. Client Bundle Secret Hygiene

- Never reference server-only credentials (`SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `DATABASE_URL`, `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, private signing keys) inside files without `import 'server-only'` or inside variables prefixed with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` / `VITE_`.
- Disable production source maps (`productionBrowserSourceMaps: false` in `next.config.*`, `build.sourcemap: false` in `vite.config.*`) unless uploaded privately to an error tracker and stripped from public CDN assets.
- Audit compiled client chunks (or run `npx github:zColdWater/vibeshield-cli <deployed-url>`) to confirm zero high-entropy tokens leak into browser bundles.

## 2. Supabase Row-Level Security (RLS) & Storage

- Every table in the `public` schema exposed through PostgREST MUST have Row-Level Security enabled (`ALTER TABLE public.<table_name> ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;`).
- Never ship permissive placeholder policies such as `USING (true)` on `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, or sensitive `SELECT`/`INSERT` operations for the `anon` role.
- Restrict `anon` grants on views and RPC functions (`SECURITY DEFINER` functions must explicitly set `search_path = public` and validate `auth.uid()`).
- Verify public vs. authenticated Supabase Storage bucket policies so user uploads cannot enumerate or overwrite other tenants' objects.

## 3. HTTP Security Headers & Transport

- Configure `Strict-Transport-Security` (`max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload`), `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`, and frame protections (`frame-ancestors 'none'` or `X-Frame-Options: DENY`).
- Avoid wildcard `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` combined with cookie or bearer authentication on API routes.
- Validate webhook signatures (Stripe, GitHub, Clerk, Supabase) against the raw unparsed request body before executing state mutations.
